From: GPT-6.1-Sol <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: gate new gadgets and release bandwidth after stop

Complete the role/teardown findings in audit 12. Store requested USB role
under the worker mutex before queueing a hardware mode. The gadget connect
path checks it so HOST->NONE cannot briefly connect a freshly registered
UDC whose initial vbus=true. Set UDC vbus after gadget creation as well as
for an existing gadget. A post-stop glue hook releases the full DDR hold
only after confirmed halt, runtime-suspended disconnect or gadget exit.
The two-second watchdog now reports a delayed stop and keeps FULL.

Local corrections to 0055/0143/0148. Lore/kernel.org searches did not find
an equivalent backport for this split legacy glue and opt-in role gate.
Hardware: HOST->NONE with worker delayed before and after mutex acquisition;
DEVICE->HOST/NONE with stop delayed over two seconds. Confirm no unintended
pullup, full vote through teardown, hub/NCM reattach and suspend/resume.

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.h b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.h
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.h
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.h
@@ -996,10 +996,12 @@
  *				need to be passed on to glue layer
  * @pre_set_role: Notify glue of role switch notifications
  * @pre_run_stop: Notify run stop enable/disable information to glue
+ * @post_gadget_stop: Notify confirmed gadget halt/teardown (sleepable)
  */
 struct dwc3_glue_ops {
 	void	(*pre_set_role)(struct dwc3 *dwc, enum usb_role role);
 	void	(*pre_run_stop)(struct dwc3 *dwc, bool is_on);
+	void	(*post_gadget_stop)(struct dwc3 *dwc);
 };
 
 /**
@@ -1073,6 +1075,8 @@
  * @role_switch_default_mode: default operation mode of controller while
  *			usb role is USB_ROLE_NONE.
  * @usb_psy: pointer to power supply interface.
+ * @role_vbus_gated: Role switch owns gadget connection state
+ * @requested_role: Latest USB role, independent of queued hardware mode
  * @vbus_draw_work: Work to set the vbus drawing limit
  * @current_limit: How much current to draw from vbus, in milliAmperes.
  * @usb2_phy: pointer to USB2 PHY
@@ -1264,6 +1268,9 @@
 	enum usb_phy_interface	hsphy_mode;
 	struct usb_role_switch	*role_sw;
 	enum usb_dr_mode	role_switch_default_mode;
+	/* Gate new gadgets, including registration before UDC vbus_work. */
+	bool			role_vbus_gated;
+	enum usb_role		requested_role;
 
 	struct power_supply	*usb_psy;
 	struct work_struct	vbus_draw_work;
@@ -1659,6 +1666,12 @@
 		dwc->glue_ops->pre_set_role(dwc, role);
 }
 
+static inline void dwc3_post_gadget_stop(struct dwc3 *dwc)
+{
+	if (dwc->glue_ops && dwc->glue_ops->post_gadget_stop)
+		dwc->glue_ops->post_gadget_stop(dwc);
+}
+
 static inline void dwc3_pre_run_stop(struct dwc3 *dwc, bool is_on)
 {
 	if (dwc->glue_ops && dwc->glue_ops->pre_run_stop)
